# Project Architecture

## Folder Structure

```
lib/
├── app/           → MaterialApp, top-level widget
├── core/          → Shared infrastructure (DI, network, storage, router, theme, widgets, utils, error, config)
├── features/      → Feature modules, each with data/ and presentation/
├── mock/          → Mock API implementations (swappable via DI environment)
└── main.dart      → Bootstrap entry point
```

## Feature Module Layout

Every feature follows this structure:

```
features/<name>/
├── data/
│   ├── models/        → Freezed data classes (*_model.dart)
│   └── repositories/  → Abstract interfaces (*_repository.dart)
└── presentation/
    ├── cubits/        → Cubit + freezed state (*_cubit.dart, *_state.dart)
    ├── pages/         → Route pages annotated with @RoutePage() (*_page.dart)
    └── widgets/       → Feature-specific widgets
```

## Rules

- New features go in `features/<name>/`, never in `core/`.
- Shared widgets go in `core/widgets/`, not duplicated per feature.
- Repositories in `data/repositories/` are abstract interfaces. Implementations live in `mock/` (or a future `data/repositories_impl/`).
- Pages only call Cubit methods and react to state. No business logic in widgets.
- `core/` code must never import from `features/`. Features may import from `core/`.
